---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const upworkUrl = 'https://www.upwork.com/services/product/writing-translation-professional-sops-and-clear-process-documentation-2098097452881572813?ref=project_share';
---
<BaseLayout title="Process Improvement & Business Operations" current="/process-improvement/" description="Process improvement, SOP program leadership, reporting, quality control, workflow improvement, documentation, and selected project services from Richard Allen.">
<section class="role-hero process-hero"><div class="container role-hero-grid">
  <div class="role-hero-copy">
    <div class="eyebrow light">Process Improvement & Business Operations</div>
    <h1>Turn scattered work into a system people can actually use.</h1>
    <p>I’m strongest when a process needs to be documented, simplified, coordinated, measured, standardized, governed, or translated into something people can repeat consistently.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button button-light" href="/case-studies/">See process case studies</a><a class="role-hero-link" href="/resume/">View résumé →</a></div>
  </div>
  <div class="before-after" aria-label="Before and after process improvement from scattered undocumented work to a governed repeatable system">
    <div class="ba-label">PROCESS TRANSFORMATION</div>
    <div class="ba-grid">
      <div class="before-side"><span>BEFORE</span><div class="scatter-stack" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><strong>Scattered</strong><small>tribal knowledge · inconsistent steps · missing ownership</small></div>
      <div class="ba-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="after-side"><span>AFTER</span><div class="system-stack"><b>STANDARD</b><b>REVIEW</b><b>OWNER</b><b>REPOSITORY</b></div><strong>Repeatable</strong><small>clear instructions · controlled updates · usable governance</small></div>
    </div>
    <div class="ba-proof"><strong>125+</strong><span>SOPs encompassed by the year-long OED modernization and governance program</span></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="process-proof-band"><div class="container process-proof-grid">
  <div><strong>125+</strong><span>SOPs encompassed by the modernization program</span></div>
  <div><strong>25+</strong><span>legacy procedures inventoried and updated</span></div>
  <div><strong>~10</strong><span>functional groups coordinated across the effort</span></div>
  <div><strong>1 year</strong><span>of sustained modernization and governance work</span></div>
</div></section>

<section class="section governance-section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Governance loop</div><h2>Improvement lasts only when ownership and maintenance are built in.</h2></div><p class="section-note">The OED work was not simply document creation; it included standards, contributor coaching, review controls, centralized storage, and a maintenance foundation.</p></div>
  <div class="governance-loop" aria-label="Process governance loop">
    <div><span>01</span><strong>Inventory</strong><small>Find what exists and what is missing.</small></div><i>→</i>
    <div><span>02</span><strong>Standardize</strong><small>Use common structure and clearer language.</small></div><i>→</i>
    <div><span>03</span><strong>Review</strong><small>Check quality, completeness, and usability.</small></div><i>→</i>
    <div><span>04</span><strong>Centralize</strong><small>Put approved work where people can find it.</small></div><i>→</i>
    <div><span>05</span><strong>Maintain</strong><small>Create ownership and update expectations.</small></div>
  </div>
  <div class="quality-strip"><div><span>QUALITY CONTROL</span><strong>Use evidence to change the process—not just coach around it.</strong></div><p>At HawkSoft, investigated a call/voicemail quality workaround, identified multiple representatives using it, coached through an action plan, and helped revise QA policy so calls of any length could be reviewed.</p></div>
</div></section>

<section class="section process-evidence-section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Process improvement in practice</div><h2>Documentation, quality, reporting, and change working together.</h2></div><p class="section-note">Selected examples from OED, HawkSoft, OHA, and The Kotter Group.</p></div>
  <div class="grid two value-grid process-card-grid">
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">125+</div><h3>SOP program leadership</h3><p>Led the year-long effort to inventory, repair, standardize, expand, centralize, and govern the SOP library. Coordinated contributors across roughly 10 functional groups, updated 25+ legacy procedures, documented missing processes, standardized templates and review controls, coached contributors, and helped centralize a program that ultimately encompassed 125+ SOPs.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-gold"><div class="card-icon">KPI</div><h3>Reporting for better decisions</h3><p>Built recurring management reporting from raw support and call data, analyzed trends, and made recommendations on staffing, training, procedures, policies/processes, and future needs; later presented most of this reporting directly to directors and upper management.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-violet"><div class="card-icon">400+</div><h3>Workforce reporting at scale</h3><p>At Oregon Health Authority, managed 400+ position records and maintained 20+ recurring and ad-hoc workforce reports while coordinating with Recruiting, HR, Classification & Compensation, Budget, DEI, and leadership.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">↻</div><h3>Change & release support</h3><p>Led staff readiness for a major HawkSoft accounting-software redesign through six months of advance communication, biweekly developer/staff education during the final two months, extra go-live support, and continued training afterward.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">CX</div><h3>Customer experience systems</h3><p>At The Kotter Group, established and managed a Customer Experience / Customer Success function, gathered customer feedback across the client base, resolved issues, created training and release documentation, and supported software functional testing and enablement.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">FLOW</div><h3>Workflow thinking</h3><p>Across support, workforce operations, implementation, and administrative work, repeatedly translated ambiguous activity into clearer handoffs, ownership, reporting, instructions, and routines people could follow.</p></article>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section project-services"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Secondary project-work pathway</div><h2>SOP & process documentation</h2></div><p class="section-note">My primary focus remains the right long-term role; selected project work is available for defined documentation needs.</p></div>
  <div class="project-service-panel">
    <div><p class="project-service-lede">If an important process is undocumented, inconsistent, outdated, or mostly living in someone’s head, I can help turn it into clear instructions your team can actually use.</p>
      <div class="service-grid"><div><strong>Standard Operating Procedures</strong><span>New SOPs built from notes, screenshots, forms, interviews, or existing materials.</span></div><div><strong>Workflow Documentation</strong><span>Who does what, when, with which inputs, decisions, systems, and handoffs.</span></div><div><strong>Training & Onboarding Guides</strong><span>Practical documentation that helps people learn and repeat the work consistently.</span></div><div><strong>Existing SOP Cleanup</strong><span>Improve clarity, consistency, organization, usability, and missing or confusing steps.</span></div><div><strong>Support-Operations Procedures</strong><span>Escalation, service, troubleshooting, quality, and support-process documentation.</span></div><div><strong>Documentation Governance</strong><span>Standards, review practices, repositories, and maintenance guidelines.</span></div></div>
    </div>
    <aside class="project-proof"><div class="eyebrow">Why this work fits</div><ul class="list-clean"><li>Year-long SOP modernization/governance program spanning 125+ SOPs, including 25+ legacy procedures inventoried and updated</li><li>Centralized repository, standards, review controls, contributor coaching, and maintenance governance</li><li>Dozens of historical HawkSoft sales policies/procedures documented</li><li>Kotter product, training, usage, release, and customer-education documentation</li></ul><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/project-work/">View project services</a><a class="button secondary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href={upworkUrl}>View Upwork SOP service</a></div></aside>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section tight"><div class="container"><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/case-studies/">See case studies</a><a class="button secondary" href="/resume/">View résumé</a><a class="button secondary" href="/contact/">Contact</a></div></div></section>

<style>
  .role-hero{padding:4.8rem 0 4rem;color:#fff;overflow:hidden}.process-hero{background:radial-gradient(circle at 84% 18%,rgba(183,121,31,.3),transparent 28%),linear-gradient(126deg,#102f55 0%,#153e75 52%,#4e477d 100%)}.role-hero-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(400px,1fr);gap:3rem;align-items:center}.role-hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.8rem,6vw,5rem);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.05em;margin:.7rem 0 1.25rem}.role-hero p{font-size:1.15rem;color:#e7edf5;max-width:720px}.role-hero-link{color:#fff;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;align-self:center}.before-after{padding:1.2rem;border-radius:24px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.08);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.18);box-shadow:0 24px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.2)}.ba-label{font-size:.72rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.15em;color:#f4dfb4;margin:.2rem 0 1rem}.ba-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto 1fr;gap:.7rem;align-items:center}.before-side,.after-side{min-height:230px;padding:1.1rem;border-radius:18px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.08);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;text-align:center}.before-side>span,.after-side>span{font-size:.68rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.13em;color:#d7e1eb}.before-side strong,.after-side strong{font-size:1.35rem;margin:.55rem 0 .2rem}.before-side small,.after-side small{color:#dfe8ef;line-height:1.4}.ba-arrow{font-size:1.8rem;color:#d9c18f}.scatter-stack{height:74px;position:relative;margin:.6rem auto 0;width:100px}.scatter-stack i{position:absolute;width:60px;height:44px;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.4);border-radius:7px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.09)}.scatter-stack i:nth-child(1){left:4px;top:18px;transform:rotate(-10deg)}.scatter-stack i:nth-child(2){left:22px;top:3px;transform:rotate(7deg)}.scatter-stack i:nth-child(3){left:34px;top:25px;transform:rotate(13deg)}.scatter-stack i:nth-child(4){left:18px;top:21px}.system-stack{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.4rem;margin:.8rem 0}.system-stack b{padding:.55rem .25rem;border-radius:8px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.11);font-size:.64rem;letter-spacing:.08em}.ba-proof{margin-top:.8rem;padding:.85rem 1rem;border-radius:14px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.08);display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.8rem}.ba-proof strong{font-size:1.9rem;color:#f0c978}.ba-proof span{font-size:.84rem;color:#e5ebf1;line-height:1.35}.process-proof-band{background:#fff;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}.process-proof-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr)}.process-proof-grid>div{padding:1.35rem;border-right:1px solid var(--border)}.process-proof-grid>div:last-child{border-right:0}.process-proof-grid strong{display:block;font-size:2rem;line-height:1;color:var(--gold)}.process-proof-grid span{display:block;margin-top:.4rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.35}.governance-section{background:linear-gradient(180deg,#fffaf1,#fff)}.governance-loop{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr;gap:.45rem;align-items:center}.governance-loop>div{min-height:165px;padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:18px;background:#fff;box-shadow:0 10px 28px rgba(23,32,42,.05)}.governance-loop span{width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;display:grid;place-items:center;background:var(--gold-soft);color:var(--gold);font-size:.7rem;font-weight:900;margin-bottom:.7rem}.governance-loop strong{display:block}.governance-loop small{display:block;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.4;margin-top:.35rem}.governance-loop>i{font-style:normal;color:#b9a06c;font-weight:900}.quality-strip{margin-top:1.2rem;padding:1.35rem;border-radius:20px;background:linear-gradient(110deg,#5b4d24,#9a6b1d);color:#fff;display:grid;grid-template-columns:.8fr 1.2fr;gap:1.5rem;align-items:center}.quality-strip span{display:block;font-size:.7rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#ffe7b0}.quality-strip strong{display:block;font-size:1.3rem;line-height:1.2;margin-top:.2rem}.quality-strip p{margin:0;color:#fff7e4}.process-evidence-section{background:#fff}.process-card-grid .card{transition:transform .18s ease,box-shadow .18s ease}.process-card-grid .card:hover{transform:translateY(-3px);box-shadow:0 15px 35px rgba(23,32,42,.08)}
  @media(max-width:1000px){.role-hero-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.governance-loop{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.governance-loop>i{display:none}.quality-strip{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
  @media(max-width:800px){.process-proof-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}
  @media(max-width:600px){.role-hero{padding:3.4rem 0}.role-hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.5rem,12vw,3.8rem)}.ba-grid,.process-proof-grid,.governance-loop{grid-template-columns:1fr}.ba-arrow{transform:rotate(90deg);text-align:center}.process-proof-grid>div{border-right:0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}.process-proof-grid>div:last-child{border-bottom:0}.ba-proof{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column;gap:.2rem}}
  @media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.process-card-grid .card{transition:none}.process-card-grid .card:hover{transform:none}}
</style>
</BaseLayout>
